### Payment Gateway — manual API walkthrough
#
# Run with VS Code's "REST Client" extension or JetBrains' built-in HTTP Client. Variables
# defined with @name are referenced as {{name}}; send the token request FIRST so the
# {{token.response.body.accessToken}} capture resolves before any other request.
#
# Prerequisite (Docker required for the bank simulator + Mongo):
#   docker compose up --build                 # full stack on localhost:5067
#   # OR (for unit / integration tests against the real services):
#   docker compose up -d bank_simulator mongo
#
# Bank simulator (imposters/bank_simulator.ejs) — last digit of card_number:
#   1, 3, 5, 7, 9 → 200 authorized=true
#   2, 4, 6, 8     → 200 authorized=false
#   0              → 503 (bank unavailable)
#
# Behaviors demonstrated end-to-end (one request per behavior, grouped by concern):
#   §1  Auth (ADR-0010) — token issuance, wrong secret (401), blank credentials (400)
#   §2  Auth gating — no token / malformed bearer both → 401
#   §3  Payment happy paths (ADR-0001) — Authorized (201), Declined (201)
#   §4  Payment failure paths — bank unavailable (503), validation rejected (400),
#       currency outside allow-list (400), amount = 0 (ADR-0002)
#   §5  GET /api/payments/{id} (ADR-0010 owner scoping) — own payment (200),
#       non-existent (404)
#   §6  Idempotency-Key (ADR-0003) — first POST cached under key, replay returns
#       same id without hitting the bank, key+different body → 422
#   §7  Metrics (ADR-0007) — Prometheus scrape emits the custom meters
#
# Behaviors NOT demonstrated via HTTP (see ADRs / working doc):
#   - ADR-0012 bank-side idempotency cache (only observable via direct simulator
#     probe, since the merchant-side filter short-circuits before the bank)
#   - ADR-0013 outbox / reconciler (background hosted service; see ADR-0013)
#   - Idempotency-Key concurrent duplicate → 409 (would need parallel requests)
#   - Cross-merchant GET → 404 (only one merchant seeded; non-existent and
#     cross-merchant share the same response shape — the test is the same one)

@host = http://localhost:5067
@demoClientId = demo-merchant
@demoClientSecret = demo-secret

###############################################################################
# §1 Auth (ADR-0010) — Mongo → CredentialCache → BCrypt → JWT issuance
###############################################################################

# @name token — send this first; subsequent requests reference its access_token.
POST {{host}}/api/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "clientId": "{{demoClientId}}",
  "clientSecret": "{{demoClientSecret}}"
}

###
# Wrong secret → 401 (uniform with unknown clientId — no existence leak between
# "wrong password" and "no such client").
POST {{host}}/api/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "clientId": "{{demoClientId}}",
  "clientSecret": "wrong-secret"
}

###
# Blank credentials → 400 (validated by FluentValidation before the credential lookup).
POST {{host}}/api/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "clientId": "",
  "clientSecret": ""
}

###############################################################################
# §2 Auth gating (ADR-0010) — every payments endpoint requires a valid bearer
###############################################################################

# No Authorization header → 401.
POST {{host}}/api/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "cardNumber": "2222405343248871",
  "expiryMonth": 12,
  "expiryYear": 2030,
  "currency": "GBP",
  "amount": 100,
  "cvv": "123"
}

###
# Malformed bearer token → 401.
GET {{host}}/api/payments/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer not-a-real-jwt

###############################################################################
# §3 Payment happy paths (ADR-0001)
###############################################################################

# @name authorized
# Card ends in 1 → bank says authorized=true. 201 Created with a Location header
# pointing at the GET route for the new Payment. id is the per-payment Guid.
POST {{host}}/api/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "cardNumber": "2222405343248871",
  "expiryMonth": 12,
  "expiryYear": 2030,
  "currency": "GBP",
  "amount": 100,
  "cvv": "123"
}

###
# @name declined
# Card ends in 2 → bank says authorized=false. 201 Created — the bank adjudicated
# (declined is a definitive answer), so the gateway persists and returns 201 with
# status=Declined. 503 (transient) is reserved for "we don't know".
POST {{host}}/api/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "cardNumber": "2222405343248872",
  "expiryMonth": 12,
  "expiryYear": 2030,
  "currency": "GBP",
  "amount": 100,
  "cvv": "123"
}

###############################################################################
# §4 Payment failure paths
###############################################################################

# Bank unavailable (card ends in 0) → 503. Nothing persisted; merchant can retry.
POST {{host}}/api/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "cardNumber": "2222405343248870",
  "expiryMonth": 12,
  "expiryYear": 2030,
  "currency": "GBP",
  "amount": 100,
  "cvv": "123"
}

###
# Validation rejected — card number too short AND expiry in the past → 400.
# FluentValidation runs before the bank is called, so no bank traffic on this path.
POST {{host}}/api/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "cardNumber": "123",
  "expiryMonth": 1,
  "expiryYear": 2020,
  "currency": "GBP",
  "amount": 100,
  "cvv": "123"
}

###
# Currency outside the configured allow-list (only GBP/USD/EUR are seeded in
# appsettings.json) → 400. The allow-list is read from config; the validator
# rejects anything not in it.
POST {{host}}/api/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "cardNumber": "2222405343248871",
  "expiryMonth": 12,
  "expiryYear": 2030,
  "currency": "XYZ",
  "amount": 100,
  "cvv": "123"
}

###
# Amount = 0 → 400 (ADR-0002 — amount must be a positive integer in the minor
# currency unit, never zero or negative).
POST {{host}}/api/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "cardNumber": "2222405343248871",
  "expiryMonth": 12,
  "expiryYear": 2030,
  "currency": "GBP",
  "amount": 0,
  "cvv": "123"
}

###############################################################################
# §5 GET /api/payments/{id} — owner scoping (ADR-0010)
###############################################################################

# Own payment (id captured from §3 authorized) → 200 with the same body.
GET {{host}}/api/payments/{{authorized.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.accessToken}}

###
# Non-existent id → 404. Same shape as the cross-merchant response (which is also
# 404, by design — owners must not be able to distinguish "doesn't exist" from
# "exists but isn't mine").
GET {{host}}/api/payments/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.accessToken}}

###############################################################################
# §6 Idempotency-Key (ADR-0003) — opt-in safe retries
###############################################################################
#
# Send the three requests separately. The first caches the response under the key;
# the second replays the cached body (bank NOT called a second time — the safety
# property); the third proves the key was bound to a specific payload.

# @name idemFirst
# First POST under key K → 201 Created. Response body (incl. id) is cached under K.
POST {{host}}/api/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111

{
  "cardNumber": "2222405343248871",
  "expiryMonth": 12,
  "expiryYear": 2030,
  "currency": "GBP",
  "amount": 100,
  "cvv": "123"
}

###
# @name idemReplay
# Same key + same body → 201 replayed from cache. id matches {{idemFirst.response.body.id}}.
# The bank is NOT called a second time (proven indirectly: this returns the cached
# id, not a fresh one — a re-call would generate a new Guid).
POST {{host}}/api/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111

{
  "cardNumber": "2222405343248871",
  "expiryMonth": 12,
  "expiryYear": 2030,
  "currency": "GBP",
  "amount": 100,
  "cvv": "123"
}

###
# @name idemHashMismatch
# Same key + different body (amount changed 100 → 999) → 422. The key was bound
# to a specific payload hash at first use; reusing it with a different payload is
# an explicit misuse the gateway rejects (rather than silently returning the wrong
# payment's result).
POST {{host}}/api/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111

{
  "cardNumber": "2222405343248871",
  "expiryMonth": 12,
  "expiryYear": 2030,
  "currency": "GBP",
  "amount": 999,
  "cvv": "123"
}

###############################################################################
# §7 Metrics (ADR-0007) — Prometheus scrape endpoint
###############################################################################
#
# Unauthenticated, intended for scraping from a trusted network. Emits the four custom
# meters defined in ADR-0007 — search the response for "payments_processed_count",
# "payments_bank_call_duration", "payments_idempotency_replay_count",
# "payments_rejected_reason_count". Counts increment after the relevant §3 / §6
# requests above; grep the response to confirm the decorated handler fired.

GET {{host}}/metrics
